00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:04.838
And a couple of people
have asked, how do you--

00:04:04.838 --> 00:04:07.850
when you work on
those problems, how

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.840
do you know you actually did it
right, or something like that?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.590
And so here, I'm going
to give you a hint.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:16.010
We design those problems
and we design them

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:20.352
typically in a way where you
can check, at least intuitively,

00:04:20.352 --> 00:04:21.560
that something good happened.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.060
Right?

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.020
Sometimes we ask
you to compare it

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.730
to some kind of simple solution.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:26.360
Right?

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.050
And then, if the simple
solution is worse than yours,

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.730
something's not right.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.450
If you're doing, let's say, a
problem on optimizing operation

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.910
of some energy storage devices
or something like that,

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.840
if you add--

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.010
so here, even if you're
in statistics, or biology,

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:44.880
doesn't matter.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.690
It should be clear that if
we give you energy storage,

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:49.950
the cost should go down.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.920
I mean, this is just completely
simple reasoning, right?

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.160
The cost should go down.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.130
So what you should
do at that point

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.070
is check that that happens.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.600
If it doesn't go down--

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.970
By the way, of course,
in some real problems,

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:05.340
you set up a problem,
and what you end up with

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.410
is not better than
some simple solution.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.032
That actually does happen.

00:05:09.032 --> 00:05:10.740
It doesn't happen here
because it kind of

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.840
undermines our message here.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.540
Also, it doesn't allow you to
check that what you're doing.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.370
So don't just do
the problem even

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.740
if it's a field outside
the one you're in.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.960
Don't do it, and then
mindlessly say, OK, there it is

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:22.800
and plot something.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.700
Just sit and think.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.330
Just give yourself five minutes
afterwards to think and go, OK.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.200
That's cool.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.100
I saved money by storing
energy when it was cheap

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.992
